# Change-handoff routing

When the user asks for a **handoff**, **impact**, or **change doc** for a **branch**, **PR**, **commit**, or **commit list/range**, delegate to the `change-handoff` subagent.

## Required doc sections

What · Why · Where (file refs with line ranges) · New flow · Impact · Verification · Gaps

## Path (always write)

Save under repo root: `docs/<scope-slug>/<change-slug>.md`

- Scope: PR → `pr-<n>`; commit/range → short tip SHA; branch/feature → kebab name; explicit override wins
- File: kebab short title; collisions get `-2`, `-3`, …
- Writable surface: handoff markdown under `docs/<scope-slug>/` only — no product-code edits

## Rules

- Prefer `rtk` + `gh` for evidence; Serena for blast radius.
- Do not paste raw full diffs into the main chat after a good handoff doc.
- Chat gets Path + short summary; full doc lives in the file.
- Not for forward-looking scouting — use `explorer` for that.
